plan.howToMeasure:
All of this was already run against patched COPIES in the scratchpad, so these are the commands that should reproduce the same numbers on the live tree after you apply the edits. Nothing here launches a browser.

Let J be /System/Library/Frameworks/JavaScriptCore.framework/Versions/A/Helpers/jsc and run from /Users/hjiang/Desktop/redalert.

1. ANCHOR CHECK BEFORE APPLYING. Every anchor in this report was verified count=1 against the live files. Re-verify any you are unsure of with python3, e.g.
   python3 -c "import io;s=io.open('js/heavyair.js',encoding='utf-8').read();print(s.count('    /* ---- C-130: the airlifter ---- */'))"
   Expect 1 for all nine. Four of the nine are INSERTs and their newCode repeats the anchor - if you see a doubled comment line after applying, that is correct and intended.

2. IT PARSES AND THE ROWS RESOLVE. Write a probe file and run:
   $J -e 'var window=this;' js/util.js js/config.js js/facts.js js/rules.js js/eras.js js/heavyair.js js/generations.js probe.js
   with probe.js containing:
     ["e50","e60","e80","e90","e00","e20"].forEach(function(e){
       print("gbr "+e+" -> "+(unitFor("gbr","heavybomber",e)||"-")+"   fra "+e+" -> "+(unitFor("fra","heavybomber",e)||"-")); });
   EXPECTED, exactly:
     gbr e50 -> gbr_e50_heavybomber   fra e50 -> -
     gbr e60 -> gbr_e60_heavybomber   fra e60 -> fra_e60_heavybomber
     gbr e80 -> gbr_e80_heavybomber   fra e80 -> fra_e80_heavybomber
     gbr e90 -> -                     fra e90 -> fra_e80_heavybomber
     gbr e00 -> -                     fra e00 -> -
     gbr e20 -> -                     fra e20 -> -
   Six filled, six empty. Any "-" where a name should be means the row was dropped; any name where a "-" should be means an era window is wrong.

3. NO DANGLING WEAPON ID (the failure that crashes at first target evaluation). Add to the probe:
     var bad=0; for(var i in UNITS){var u=UNITS[i]; if(!u.weapons)continue;
       for(var q=0;q<u.weapons.length;q++) if(!WEAPONS[u.weapons[q]]) {print("DANGLING "+i+" -> "+u.weapons[q]); bad++;} }
     print("dangling: "+bad);
   EXPECTED: dangling: 0. It is 0 on the current tree and 0 on the patched one.

4. THE POOL AND THE HELD ROUND, which is where the design lives. Add:
     ["gbr_e50_heavybomber","gbr_e60_heavybomber","gbr_e80_heavybomber","fra_e60_heavybomber","fra_e80_heavybomber"].forEach(function(k){
       var u=UNITS[k]; print(k+" ammo="+u.ammo+" sight="+u.sight+" radius="+u.radius);
       u.weapons.forEach(function(w){var W=WEAPONS[w];
         print("   "+W.name+" dmg "+W.dmg+" rng "+W.range+" acc "+W.acc+" burst "+(W.burst||1)+" ammo "+W.ammo+" manual "+!!W.manual);});});
   EXPECTED, measured:
     gbr_e50 ammo=6 sight=9  radius=78 | Blue Danube dmg 520 rng 2.2 acc 0.66 burst 1 ammo 6 manual true
     gbr_e60 ammo=6 sight=9  radius=86 | Yellow Sun Mk.2 dmg 720 rng 2.2 acc 0.641 burst 1 ammo 6 manual true
     gbr_e80 ammo=6 sight=9  radius=86 | 21 x 1,000lb dmg 140 rng 2.2 acc 0.552 burst 7 ammo 2 manual false
     fra_e60 ammo=6 sight=9  radius=46 | AN-22 dmg 600 rng 2 acc 0.678 burst 1 ammo 6 manual true
     fra_e80 ammo=6 sight=10.7 radius=46 | ASMP dmg 660 rng 10.4 acc 0.898 burst 1 ammo 6 manual true
   THE NUMBERS THAT PROVE IT: every ammo is 6 (generations.js floors heavybomber at 6, so nothing was silently rewritten); the three nuclear rounds cost 6 against a pool of 6, which is exactly one weapon per sortie; Black Buck costs 2 against 6, which is three sticks of seven = 21 bombs; manual is true on the three nuclear rounds and FALSE on the iron bombs; fra_e80's sight has grown itself from 9 to 10.7 to match the ASMP's 10.4. The acc values shifted off the written figures (0.64->0.641, 0.55->0.552, 0.68->0.678, 0.88->0.898) because generations.js DOMAIN cloned them - if you see the raw written values instead, the clone did not happen and something in generations.js changed.

5. NOTHING ELSE MOVED. The strongest check. Snapshot every faction x role x era answer before and after:
   put this in snap.js -
     var FACS=["nato","pact","pla","kpa","gbr","fra","deu","roc"], ES=["e50","e60","e80","e90","e00","e20"];
     var roles={}; for(var i in UNITS) if(UNITS[i].role) roles[UNITS[i].role]=1;
     Object.keys(roles).sort().forEach(function(r){FACS.forEach(function(f){ES.forEach(function(e){
       print(f+"|"+r+"|"+e+"="+(unitFor(f,r,e)||"-"));});});});
     var n=0; for(var w in WEAPONS)n++; print("WEAPONCOUNT "+n);
     var m=0; for(var u in UNITS)m++; print("UNITCOUNT "+m);
   Run it on git stash (before) and on the applied tree (after) and diff the two outputs.
   EXPECTED DIFF, and nothing else: 6 changed unitFor lines (gbr heavybomber e50/e60/e80, fra heavybomber e60/e80/e90), UNITCOUNT 1202 -> 1207, WEAPONCOUNT 1784 -> 1793. The weapon count goes up by 9 rather than 5 because generations.js clones four of the five for the DOMAIN pass. If the diff contains any other line, something collided.

6. THE BEHAVIOUR SUITE. _behtest.html, in your browser, must still read 89 passed / 0 failed. I have not run it and cannot. This is the one number I am asking you to measure that I could not.

7. THE SILHOUETTES. Open the game or airsheet.html at e50, e60 and e80 as Britain and at e60 and e80 as France. What proves the air_specs rows landed: the Vulcan is a tailless delta with one fin and NO tailplane, four nozzles in two pairs at the wing roots and no engine pods under the wing; the Valiant has a tailplane at the top of the fin and exactly one of them, not a second low on the body; the Mirage IV is a small area-ruled delta with cheek intakes, not a B-52. If any of them looks like a B-52, the air_specs.js edit did not apply.
